# Rime scene v1 (.rscene) — reflection-serialized world. Human-diffable; hand-edit or regenerate.
# m16.10 big-asset proof: four CC0 Poly Haven assets at vehicle and machine scale, with the
# three m16.9 props in the foreground as a size reference.
#
# WHERE THE VIEWPOINT COMES FROM, because it is not obvious and cost three renders to pin
# down: 99-the-block REQUIRES a Camera entity (it exits 1 with "the block's scene carries no
# camera"), but it does NOT look through it -- the player controller owns the view and spawns
# at roughly (-6, 1.6, 0) facing +X, which puts +Z on the viewer's RIGHT. So everything here
# is laid out along +X and spread in depth; a layout down -Z renders perfectly, off-screen.
#
# Y offsets are each GLB's measured POSITION bounds, so nothing floats or sinks: the ship's
# hull sits 1.92 m low in its own model space and the crane's gantry legs 3.91 m.
# overhead_crane IS fetched, exported and cooked, but is deliberately NOT placed here: its
# 'overhead_crane_trim' material binds image 1 -- overhead_crane_trim_MASK -- as baseColorTexture,
# because Poly Haven builds that trim sheet from a mask-driven procedural node graph rather than a
# texture-to-PBR-slot chain, and the glTF exporter has no colour map to pick. It renders as
# saturated mask noise. See docs/authoring-blender.md; evidence crane-mask-bug.png.
rime_scene 1

entity 0 {
  rime::ecs::LocalTransform 0xe7d60f5a66770fe9 {
    value {
      translation { x -6 y 1.7 z 0 }
      rotation { x 0.0000000 y 0.7071068 z 0.0000000 w 0.7071068 }
      scale { x 1.0 y 1.0 z 1.0 }
    }
  }
  rime::render::Camera 0x42cdb0b7ddc97dbc {
    fov_y 0.87266
    z_near 0.1
    z_far 1000
    active true
  }
}

